{
  "_comment": [
    "Presentation metadata Sextant owns, merged over the option tree at catalog",
    "export (ADR 0019). It exists because half the settings surface is defined",
    "in DAWO-NixOS upstream, where a label needs a fork and a merge request -",
    "so on 2026-08-06 an operator read a settings page where 36 of 69 options",
    "showed as raw dotted paths like desktop.gnome.enable.",
    "",
    "An UPSTREAM label always wins. An entry here is a catch-up, not a second",
    "source of truth: when the core labels an option properly, delete the entry",
    "and the orphan check will tell you if you forgot.",
    "",
    "widget is only for what a TYPE cannot imply - a string that is really a",
    "from and a to, a list that is really a few named slots. Booleans, enums,",
    "integers and open-ended lists need nothing here."
  ],
